From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:40:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fontsub: Make subsets of TrueType fonts as Windows makes
 them.

CreateFontPackage copied the whole font for any subset.  Office asks for
one whenever it embeds a font: Word's PDF export of a page of text
embedded all of DengXian, twice, and wrote 19 MB; a document saved with
its fonts embedded carried 16 MB for a few characters.

A subset now keeps the font's glyph indices, as Windows's does, so that
what refers to glyphs by index still works: the glyphs it does not keep
lose their outlines and characters and every other table stays.  What
it keeps besides the glyphs or characters asked for is what Windows
keeps, as tools/fontsubprobe in the outer tree measured it: the first
three glyphs, the justification extenders, the glyphs of '"', 'M', 'd'
and 'r' when a list is given, the components of composite glyphs and
every glyph a substitution can make.

The tables are rewritten the way Windows rewrites them, measured by
subsetting the same fonts with both on Windows and comparing the files:
glyf with each outline padded to two bytes and loca short when it fits;
hmtx and vmtx with long metrics up to the glyph after the last kept one
and none for the others, or as they were when all are still needed;
LTSH and hdmx with nothing for the glyphs that go; the cmap subtables of
formats 0, 4, 6, 12 and 13 with the characters of kept glyphs, glyph 0
mapping nothing, on even offsets, the old one kept when the new one
would be larger and format 14 left as it is; maxp's maximums from the
kept glyphs, fpgm and prep; kern with the pairs of kept glyphs, gone
when none are left; EBLC and EBDT with the index subtables that hold
kept glyphs, cut to them, formats 1 and 3 as 3, a run of one size as a
list unless the kept glyphs follow each other, bitmaps shared between
sizes kept shared, a size dropped when its bitmaps outgrow format 3 and
both tables gone when no size is left; post without glyph names; name
with each string inside the longest one holding it; OS/2's range of
characters only when a subtable of the Microsoft platform was rebuilt
on its own.  The tables Windows places itself go in its order, the
others in an order of Windows's that is not understood, as near as the
fonts measured allow.  A face of a collection is
made a font of its own.  Without TTFCFP_FLAGS_SUBSET nothing is made or
written, and the parameter errors are Windows's; a font without maxp
has no glyphs.

Of 48 subsets of Windows's and free fonts, among them SimSun, MS Gothic,
Arial, Segoe UI and Segoe UI Emoji, 44 have every table the same as
Windows's, 12 of them byte for byte and the others with the tables in
another order.  The rest differ in where name keeps three strings, for
a reason not found, and in Gentium's Macintosh cmap, where Windows puts
each glyph at the wrong character when the subtable does not start at
0.

MergeFontPackage copies a working font; merging and the formats that
merge are left to do.  The export of that page is now 39 KB, and looks
the same.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 1bf949b4b75d292a2f52c01fdba2bb4a570b59fc)

